{"amendments":[{"body":"Surface `valid_range` diagnostics from the normal process-parameter loader. `load_process_params()` only deserializes and runs `validate()` ([crates/tank_data/src/lib.rs:65-74]), while the new warning path lives in `ProcessParamsPreset::check_ranges()` ([crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:662-667]) and is never called there. In practice, an out-of-range or malformed `valid_range` loads silently in production, so the acceptance criterion for an explicit warning/diagnostic path is not actually met.","rationale":"Right now the provenance metadata is write-only unless every caller remembers to run a second helper manually; bad scientific ranges will be missed during ordinary preset loading."},{"body":"Do not silently renormalize legacy `_mg` / `_mg_total` fields unless the metadata explicitly opts into that conversion. `provenance_value()` always rewrites the stored value before formatting or range checks ([crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:635-641]), and `legacy_process_param_normalization()` hard-codes fields like `aob_k_tan_mg` and `decomposer_k_doc_mg` to `mg/L` (or `mg/m²` for one plant special case) regardless of the supplied unit string ([crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:896-937]). With the shipped preset, `aob_k_tan_mg` is serialized as `0.5` ([crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml:29-32]), but `format_param()` can emit `0.025` with no unit/source metadata at all ([crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:644-657]). That makes both the developer-facing formatter and `valid_range` warnings misleading for legacy-unit metadata, and there is no opt-out if an author wants provenance expressed in the serialized units.","rationale":"A provenance formatter that changes the numeric value behind the user's back is a correctness problem: reports/debug output can disagree with the file being reviewed."},{"body":"Extend the adjacent per-parameter metadata slot beyond `ProcessParamsPreset`. The new schema is only attached to process coefficients ([crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:503-508]); `SourceWaterPreset` still exposes only file-level `provenance` ([crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:29-49]) and `ShrimpPreset` does the same ([crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:142-185]). That means the task still cannot carry per-parameter source/confidence/range metadata for source-water chemistry or shrimp-life-history parameters without another schema/API change, which falls short of the requested chemistry-and-biology coverage.","rationale":"The next provenance-enrichment beads need those data families too; stopping at process presets leaves the schema incomplete and guarantees another round of compatibility work."}],"summary":"Reviewed the actual `tanksim-6e5.7.1` provenance implementation (the live worktree itself had no uncommitted diff). Targeted `tank_data` / `tank_core` tests pass, but I found three substantive gaps: normal loads never surface `valid_range` warnings, the formatter/range checker silently renormalize legacy values in a misleading way, and per-parameter metadata is still limited to process presets."}